    "body": "- [ X ] This PR does not suggest changes based on personal taste (enabling new or changing value of existing option, install new plugin)\r\n\r\nThe first commit is a bug fix to avoid `<Leader>eq` from messing with loclist windows.\r\n\r\nThe second commit adds `<Leader>el` to toggle the loclist in a similar manner to `<Leader>eq`.",
    "closed_at": "2026-01-08T13:29:55Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nThe general idea is for this type of functionality to be handled in planned 'mini.quickfix'. But as it is not the high priority right now, there is a simple helper to toggle quickfix window (since I find it really useful).\r\n\r\nI guess it does make sense to make it less intrusive with respect to the location list. But my concern here is to get as less elaborate helper function as possible.\r\n\r\n> The first commit is a bug fix to avoid `<Leader>eq` from messing with loclist windows.\r\n\r\nCan you please be more specific (as I rarely use location lists)? Judging by the commit's change, the problem is that `<Leader>eq` can close the location list? I think my expectation here would be to \"act on location list if it is available for current window, otherwise - quickfix list\".\r\n\r\nOr maybe indeed it might make sense to have a separate mapping for location list... Oddly enough, I think the `<Leader>eQ` might make more sense, since there are many places that have \"lower letter for global scope, upper letter for narrower scope\". I'll have to think about this.",
            "created_at": "2026-01-05T15:44:07Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/pull/27#issuecomment-3710960533",
            "id": 3710960533,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-mini/MiniMax/issues/27",
            "minimized": null,
            "node_id": "IC_kwDOP9V4Js7dMMOV",
            "performed_via_github_app": null,
