        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I can see eQ as a suitable alternative, although I think the native bindings `[l` and `]l`, etc., and the `:lhelp` and `:lgrep`, etc. commands, mean that it would be confusing to use Q just for Mini. Probably your first instinct, that it's not a frequently used feature so it can be left out, is best.\r\n\r\nYes, the mismatch is the only thing that keeps me from adding `<Leader>eQ` right now. I still like it because addressing quickfix and not loclist is somewhat incomplete while `<Leader>el` is a valuable \"keymap real estate\" :)",
