        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be resolved on latest `main`. After a bit of research, there appears to be a [more concise and robust way](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/blob/a42705c2a213f27039587da9901b9af464ed6f30/configs/nvim-0.11/plugin/20_keymaps.lua#L104-L109) of implementing \"explore/toggle quickfix/location list\" mappings.\r\n\r\nI also did end up deciding to go with `<Leader>eQ`. Partially to follow the other `<Leader>` keymaps of \"global/local\" <-> \"lower/upper\" direction. Partially due to the realization that built-in (and 'mini.bracketed') `[q` / `]q` were the first to not follow the `:copen` / `:cnext` / `:cprev` / `:cclose` command prefix.\r\n\r\nThank you again for noticing this and making PR!",
